title: M5_SAVE_LOAD_START
---
<<declare $m5_save_number = 10.5>>
<<declare $m5_save_flag = true>>
<<declare $m5_save_text = "STATE_A">>

<<vn_bg m3_bg_a>>
<<vn_clear_cg>>
<<vn_show m3_a default left>>
<<vn_facing m3_a right>>
<<vn_scale m3_a 1.0>>
<<bgm_play m4_bgm_a>>
<<jump M5_CHECKPOINT_A>>
===

title: M5_CHECKPOINT_A
---
<<vn_checkpoint m5_checkpoint_a>>
M5 CHECKPOINT A RESUMED/ACTIVE — number {$m5_save_number}, flag {$m5_save_flag}, text {$m5_save_text}.

Save State A: open Save > Manual, select Slot 1, and verify its metadata and thumbnail. For Quick Save, use Save > Quick and select its only slot.

Advance to create visibly and audibly different State B.

<<set $m5_save_number = 99.25>>
<<set $m5_save_flag = false>>
<<set $m5_save_text = "STATE_B">>
<<vn_bg m3_bg_b>>
<<vn_clear_cg>>
<<vn_expression m3_a smile>>
<<vn_move m3_a right>>
<<vn_facing m3_a left>>
<<vn_scale m3_a 1.1>>
<<bgm_play m4_bgm_b>>
<<jump M5_CHECKPOINT_B>>
===

title: M5_CHECKPOINT_B
---
<<vn_checkpoint m5_checkpoint_b>>
M5 CHECKPOINT B ACTIVE — number {$m5_save_number}, flag {$m5_save_flag}, text {$m5_save_text}.

Load test: open Load > Manual and load Slot 1 to resume State A. Quick test: save here with Save > Quick; after advancing to A, Load > Quick restores this latest State B.

Autosave rotation: advance to re-enter A, then advance again for B. Six total checkpoint entries exercise all five Auto slots and one overwrite.

<<set $m5_save_number = 10.5>>
<<set $m5_save_flag = true>>
<<set $m5_save_text = "STATE_A">>
<<vn_bg m3_bg_a>>
<<vn_clear_cg>>
<<vn_expression m3_a default>>
<<vn_move m3_a left>>
<<vn_facing m3_a right>>
<<vn_scale m3_a 1.0>>
<<bgm_play m4_bgm_a>>
<<jump M5_CHECKPOINT_A>>
===
